Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A paid POST on all three routes answers 202 Accepted with a pollUrl; the SDK
returned that envelope while its docstrings and README promised assetUrl and
provenance, so `track["assetUrl"]` raised KeyError on every live call.

- create_music / agent_video / agent_image now poll the unpriced pollUrl until
  the render finishes (model_version leaves pending; status is completed or
  failed) and return the asset URL. wait=False returns the queued envelope;
  poll_song / poll_job collect later. RenderTimeout carries the poll URL.
- Every paid POST sends X-Idempotency-Key, one UUID per intended purchase,
  reused on the paid retry, so a timed-out retry cannot buy a second render.
- create_music sends only the published request fields (prompt, style,
  lyrics, custom_mode, make_instrumental, vocal_gender, tags);
  duration_seconds is deprecated and no longer sent.
- select_requirement accepts the `base` network alias and prefers eip155:8453.
- Tests rebuilt from the published contract (42 passing); README documents
  the asynchronous flow. Version 0.5.0.

Contract: https://github.com/JasonColapietro/suede-x402
