-The first call returns 402 with the x402-v2 challenge. The SDK signs an EIP-3009 `transferWithAuthorization` for USDC on Base, replays with `PAYMENT-SIGNATURE`, and returns the JSON body. You never touch the typed data.
+The first call returns 402 with the x402-v2 challenge. The SDK signs an EIP-3009 `transferWithAuthorization` for USDC on Base and replays with `PAYMENT-SIGNATURE`. The paid call answers `202 Accepted` with a poll URL — renders take minutes — so the SDK then polls that URL (free, no second payment) until the render finishes and hands back the asset. You never touch the typed data or the poll loop.
+
+## Asynchronous renders
+
+Every paid call is asynchronous by default on all three routes. The media methods wait for you:
+
+| Method | Paid response | Polls | Finished when | Result |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `create_music` | `202` + `pollUrl` | `GET /api/songs/{songId}` | `model_version` leaves `pending` | `{"status", "songId", "shareUrl", "pollUrl", "audioUrl", "modelVersion", "song"}` |
+| `agent_video` | `202` + `pollUrl` | `GET /agent/video/{jobId}` | `status` is `completed` | the final job envelope with `videoUrl` |
+| `agent_image` | `202` + `pollUrl` | `GET /agent/image/{jobId}` | `status` is `completed` | the final job envelope with `imageUrl` |
+
+A failed render comes back as `status: "failed"` rather than an exception; the charge already happened when the job was created.
+
+Pass `wait=False` to return as soon as the job is queued and collect later:
+
+```python
+queued = suede.create_music(prompt="slow-burn desert rock", wait=False)
+row = suede.poll_song(queued["pollUrl"])      # or suede.poll_job(url) for video/image
+```
+
+`poll_interval` (default 5s) and `poll_timeout` (default 600s) are constructor and per-call arguments. When the timeout passes, `suede_ai.RenderTimeout` is raised carrying `poll_url`; the purchase stands and you can keep polling.
+
+Every paid `POST` carries an `X-Idempotency-Key` (a fresh UUID per call, or pass `idempotency_key=` to control it). Reuse one key across every retry of the same purchase and the server replays the original response instead of charging again.
 
